		{
			"id": "link-3293eb0f037addf5466f9d97352c19b5",
			"title": "Ask HN: I have been unemployed for 2y. 15 years of experience, US. What to do?",
			"link": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50583761",
			"contents": "<div class=\"Story_container\"><div class=\"Story_data\"><div class=\"Story_title\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50583761\"><span>Ask HN: I have been unemployed for 2y. 15 years of experience, US. What to do?</span></a></div><div class=\"Story_meta\"><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50583761\">754 points</a></span><span class=\"Story_separator\">|</span><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=LetThingsBeDiff\"><span>LetThingsBeDiff</span></a></span><span class=\"Story_separator\">|</span><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50583761\">7 days ago</a></span><span class=\"Story_separator\">|</span><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50583761\">867 comments</a></span><div class=\"Story_comment\"><span>I'm Senior software engineer in the US (DMV area), with 15y of experience. Worked for Fortune 50+ company and bunch of mid-size companies. Been unemployed for 2y and can't find a job, within those 2 years, I pretty much spent my savings that I've saved through years, maybe have 4-5 months left to support my household. Currently, I tutor math and probably about to start working as manager in pizzaria.<p>In Jan 2025, I quit from a mid-size insurance tech company(1000+) after working there for almost 4y, because I was tipped off the they were about to start layoffs and they did. Well, since then I have zero luck finding any job in SWE.</p><p>At this point, I have massive gap in my resume that I can't explain to recruiters, I can still code (C#/.NET/AWS) and learned the AI, but who cares if date of my last employment is Jan2025. What should I do ?</p><p>If you have an alternative path (something completely different from SWE or SWE adjacent) that pays \"well\", I would like to hear.</p></span></div></div></div></div>",
			"retrieved": 1795544120902
		},
